      "message": "This one does not reach the export. Quill sanitises a link when it builds\nthe line, and `getContents()` reads the attributes back from the DOM, so the\nexporter is given what was displayed, never what was sent.\n\nProbed on the shipped bundle, with the hostile attribute written straight into\nthe CRDT the way a replica that does not run our code would (going through our\nown writer would only test what we send):\n\n    sent : javascript:alert(1)\n    DOM  : about:blank\n    html : \u003ca href\u003d\"about:blank\"\u003eclick\u003c/a\u003e\n    md   : [click](about:blank)\n\nSame for `JaVaScRiPt:`, `data:text/html,...` and `vbscript:`. Quill\u0027s\n`PROTOCOL_WHITELIST` is `[\"http\", \"https\", \"mailto\", \"tel\", \"sms\"]`; everything\nelse becomes `about:blank`.\n\nYou are right that it should not rest on knowing this: patch set 3 adds a test\nthat writes each of those four schemes into the document as a peer and asserts\nthat neither the DOM nor either export carries them.",
      "parentUuid": "88b2e263_71f8c0bd",
      "revId": "30f6603ef42097cf10ff8cb194d89da88d39ffcd",
      "serverId": "1e26b4c1-6b8c-47ff-9df7-501b633d3b5a"
    },
